-- title:
--   Lemma 2.1 — the cycle space of $G_r$ is generated by short cycles
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a graph, $r\in\mathbb N$, and let $p_r:G_r\to G$ be the $r$-local covering of $G$. Then the binary cycle space of $G_r$ is generated by its cycles of length at most $r$: for every cycle $O$ of $G_r$ there are cycles $O_1,\dots,O_n$ of $G_r$ of length $\le r$ with
--   $$E(O)=E(O_1)\,\triangle\,\cdots\,\triangle\,E(O_n).$$
--
--   The paper cites this from [DJKK26, Lemma 4.6] and uses it implicitly whenever a correspondence between local and global notions is applied in $G_r$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the r-local covering $p_r : G_r \to G$, unique up to isomorphism of coverings → an arbitrary covering $p : C \to G$ with `IsLocalCovering G r p` (characteristic subgroup = the r-local subgroup), on a vertex type in the universe of $V$; reason: the paper constructs $G_r$ only up to isomorphism; every statement holds for one such covering iff for all, and one exists in the universe of $V$ (walks modulo the r-local subgroup)
--   - reading: the binary cycle space of $G$ is generated by cycles of length $\le r$ → every cycle's edge set is a finite symmetric difference of edge sets of cycles of length $\le r$ (`CycleSpaceGenByShort`); reason: the finite cycle space; the proofs (Lemma 4.3, Correspondence 4.4) argue with finite $\mathbb Z/2$ sums
-- source:
--   Jacobs, Knappe, Kurkofka, Canonical Graph Decompositions via Local Separations, preprint (STOC 2027 submission, arXiv:2501.16170; sha256 9a11d48d…), Lemma 2.1, p.13 (citing [DJKK26, Lemma 4.6])

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LocalSepDecomp_Cutouts

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace LocalSepDecomp

open SimpleGraph

universe u

/-- **Lemma 2.1** ([DJKK26, Lemma 4.6]). R. W. Jacobs, P. Knappe, J. Kurkofka, *Canonical Graph Decompositions via Local Separations*,
preprint (STOC 2027 submission, arXiv:2501.16170; sha256 9a11d48d…), Lemma 2.1, p.13.
The binary cycle space of the `r`-local covering `G_r` is generated by its short cycles (cycles of
length `≤ r`).

**Formalization Note.** `G_r` is any `p : C → G` with `IsLocalCovering G r p`. The cycle space is
the finite one (`CycleSpaceGenByShort`). -/
theorem lemma_2_1 {V W : Type u} (G : SimpleGraph V) (r : ℕ) (C : SimpleGraph W) (p : C →g G)
    (hp : IsLocalCovering G r p) : CycleSpaceGenByShort C r := by sorry

end LocalSepDecomp
